      "snippet": "They found that the majority of studies reported no difference in costs and efficiency between public and private provision and some studies even concluded that public provision of the services was cheaper.6 • Similarly, in 2007, Roland Zullo found in his research that governments gained no immediate or long-term economic benefit from contracted bus services.7 This finding was substantiated in 2009 by Suzanne Leland and Olga Smirnova who found that privately owned and managed transit systems are not more efficient or more effective than government owned agencies.8 What Experience Shows The actual experiences of cities and states that have privatized public functions mirror the findings presented in the research above.",
